WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.001
Rhetorical Synthesis

00:00:02.381 --> 00:00:05.378
Read the goal first. The notes come last.

00:00:06.579 --> 00:00:07.577
How to spot it

00:00:07.977 --> 00:00:09.489
A bulleted list of notes

00:00:10.039 --> 00:00:12.212
The question says “the student wants to…”

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:16.551
It’s testing: choosing information for a specific job

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:18.546
The method

00:00:18.946 --> 00:00:21.373
Step 1: Read the question first

00:00:21.653 --> 00:00:23.034
Skip the notes for now.

00:00:23.584 --> 00:00:25.685
Step 2: Underline the goal

00:00:25.965 --> 00:00:27.616
The action and what it’s about.

00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:30.141
Step 3: Make a checklist

00:00:30.421 --> 00:00:33.285
Two bridges? A difference? About length?

00:00:33.835 --> 00:00:35.943
Step 4: Tick every box

00:00:36.223 --> 00:00:38.134
Only one choice does the whole job.

00:00:38.684 --> 00:00:39.794
In a few words

00:00:39.944 --> 00:00:42.857
Goal. Checklist. Tick every box.

00:00:44.057 --> 00:00:44.996
Goal words

00:00:45.396 --> 00:00:46.278
Similarity

00:00:46.558 --> 00:00:48.314
Both items + what they share.

00:00:48.864 --> 00:00:49.700
Difference

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.808
Both items + how they differ.

00:00:52.358 --> 00:00:53.724
Unfamiliar audience

00:00:54.004 --> 00:00:55.797
Explain the unfamiliar term.

00:00:56.347 --> 00:00:58.162
Aim, method, finding

00:00:58.442 --> 00:01:03.342
Aim = why. Method = how. Finding = what they found.

00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:05.583
Let’s try one

00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:10.167
The Akashi Kaikyō Bridge in Japan opened in 1998.

00:01:10.547 --> 00:01:14.601
Its central span is 1,991 meters long.

00:01:14.981 --> 00:01:19.484
The Golden Gate Bridge in the United States opened in 1937.

00:01:19.864 --> 00:01:23.756
Its central span is 1,280 meters long.

00:01:24.136 --> 00:01:25.811
Both are suspension bridges.

00:01:26.361 --> 00:01:31.449
While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:

00:01:31.449 --> 00:01:36.949
The student wants to emphasize a difference in the lengths of the two bridges’ central spans.

00:01:36.949 --> 00:01:42.490
Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.815
The goal: emphasize a difference in the lengths of the two spans.

00:01:47.815 --> 00:01:51.672
Your checklist: two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:01:52.224 --> 00:01:57.507
Cross out A, a similarity; B, a difference in dates;

00:01:57.507 --> 00:02:00.289
and D, which mentions only one bridge.

00:02:00.839 --> 00:02:05.039
C ticks every box: two bridges, a difference, and length.

00:02:06.239 --> 00:02:07.234
Common traps

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:08.861
True but off-task

00:02:09.141 --> 00:02:11.304
Accurate, but does a different job.

00:02:11.854 --> 00:02:12.753
Half the goal

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.157
Ticks one box, misses another.

00:02:16.357 --> 00:02:17.757
Rhetorical Synthesis

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.951
Goal. Checklist. Tick every box.

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:22.274
Spot it

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:24.941
Bulleted notes + “The student wants to…”

00:02:25.491 --> 00:02:26.198
Steps

00:02:26.398 --> 00:02:28.315
1. Read the question first

00:02:28.595 --> 00:02:30.265
2. Underline the goal

00:02:30.545 --> 00:02:32.102
3. Make a checklist

00:02:32.382 --> 00:02:35.050
4. Pick the choice that ticks every box

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:36.352
Remember

00:02:36.552 --> 00:02:39.758
Similarity: both items + what they share

00:02:40.038 --> 00:02:43.009
Difference: both items + how they differ

00:02:43.289 --> 00:02:45.523
New audience: explain the term

00:02:45.803 --> 00:02:49.700
Aim = why, method = how, finding = result

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:50.855
Trap

00:02:51.055 --> 00:02:53.112
True, but does a different job

00:02:53.862 --> 00:02:57.557
